\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{frap}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{When a character is conserved}

\p{For finite #{I}, the ambient coordinate group
#{W=K\wr\operatorname{Sym}(I)} has the
\vocabk{total-orientation character}{frap-000S}
#{\chi(\pi,a)=\prod_i[a_i]\in K_{\mathrm{ab}}}. If a puzzle's
allowed moves form a set #{S\subseteq W}, its legal group is
#{G=\langle S\rangle}, usually a proper subgroup of #{W}. Then}
##{G\subseteq\ker\chi\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
    \chi(s)=1\quad\hbox{for every }s\in S.}
\p{The forward implication includes each generator. Conversely the
kernel of a homomorphism is a subgroup, so it contains all products and
inverses of generators lying in it. This is the generator-check step
discussed after the canonical character in
\citet{Section 3.1, p. 7}{marchetti2025rubik}. Its premise must be
verified for the chosen moves.}

\p{The nonabelian product of local factors need not be independent of
order or frames. Abelianization makes reindexing and frame cancellation
valid, but neither of those operations says that #{\chi(s)=1}.
The \vocabk{cycle criterion}{frap-000U} supplies a sufficient test,
applied explicitly to \vocabk{cube face turns}{frap-000V}.}
